      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(¬X∧¬Y)$ using De Morgan's laws.",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(X∧Y)≡¬X∨¬Y, \\\\ ¬(X∨Y)≡¬X∧¬Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬X∧¬Y) & ≡¬(¬X)∨¬(¬Y) \\\\  & ≡X∨Y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
