      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Rewrite the statement $¬(M∨(¬M∧¬N))$ using De Morgan's laws.",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∧B)≡¬A∨¬B, \\\\ ¬(A∨B)≡¬A∧¬B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(M∨(¬M∧¬N)) & ≡¬M∧¬(¬M∧¬N) \\\\  & ≡¬M∧(¬(¬M)∨¬(¬N)) \\\\  & ≡¬M∧(M∨N)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
